PROJECT TITLE:

MY PERSONAL PURPOSE, VISION & DIRECTION BLUEPRINT

This is the major practical assignment for Module 3.

The learner must produce a document that converts personal reflection into a structured direction and action plan.

PART A — PERSONAL CONTEXT

Describe:

Who you are;

Your current life/career/business situation;

Your major responsibilities;

Your current strengths;

Your major challenges;

Your current opportunities.

Maximum recommended length: 500–750 words.

PART B — PURPOSE DISCOVERY

Document:

What matters to you;

Your strongest capabilities;

Capabilities you can develop;

Problems you care about;

People/markets/institutions you want to serve;

Contribution you want to make.

Then produce your:

PERSONAL PURPOSE STATEMENT

One clear paragraph.

PART C — PERSONAL VISION

Write a compelling but realistic description of the future you want to build.

Cover:

Character;

Capability;

Career;

Business where relevant;

Finances;

Relationships;

Health;

Service;

Impact;

Legacy.

Then produce a concise:

PERSONAL VISION STATEMENT

PART D — 3–5 YEAR DIRECTION

Identify the major outcomes you want to achieve within approximately 3–5 years.

For each:

Desired outcome;

Why it matters;

Capabilities required;

Resources required;

Major risks;

Indicators of progress.

PART E — 1-YEAR GOALS

Select no more than 5–7 major annual goals.

For every goal provide:

Goal

Reason

Measure

Deadline

Required capabilities

Resources

Potential obstacles

First major action

PART F — 90-DAY OBJECTIVES

Convert the annual goals into a maximum of three major 90-day outcomes.

For each:

Objective

Success measure

Deadline

Weekly actions

Required resources

Evidence

PART G — PERSONAL DEVELOPMENT PLAN

Identify your most important capability gaps.

For each gap:

Current capability → Desired capability → Learning → Practice → Application → Feedback → Evidence

PART H — PRIORITY SYSTEM

Create your personal priority list.

My three most important priorities for the next 90 days:

Things I should stop or reduce:

Things I should delegate or seek help with:

Things I must protect time for:

PART I — PERSONAL SCORECARD

Create five to ten measurable indicators.

Examples:

Courses completed;

Projects completed;

Income;

Savings;

Customers;

Applications;

Interviews;

Professional connections;

Books studied;

Hours practised;

Business revenue;

Customer satisfaction;

Productivity;

Fitness consistency.

