PART J — WEEKLY ACCOUNTABILITY SYSTEM

Create a weekly review schedule.

Every week answer:

What did I plan?

What did I complete?

What result did I produce?

What did I fail to complete?

Why?

What did I learn?

What will I change?

What are next week's three priorities?

PART K — PERSONAL COMMITMENT

Write a short commitment statement explaining:

What you are committing to;

What you will stop doing;

What you will start doing;

How you will measure yourself;

Who can hold you accountable.

A project should not receive a high score merely because it is beautifully written.

The question is:

Does this blueprint give the learner a credible direction and a practical system for moving toward it?

Assessors should look for:

Clarity;

Authenticity;

Strategic thinking;

Measurable outcomes;

Realistic planning;

Appropriate prioritization;

Capability development;

Evidence;

Practical action.

PERSONAL

Use purpose and vision to guide:

Lifestyle;

Relationships;

Learning;

Finances;

Personal development.

CAREER

Use them to guide:

Career choices;

Skill development;

Professional positioning;

Networking;

Advancement.

BUSINESS

Use them to guide:

Market selection;

Products;

Services;

Customers;

Strategy;

Investments;

Hiring;

Growth.

GOVERNMENT

Use them to guide:

Public priorities;

Policy objectives;

Programmes;

Resource allocation;

Service delivery;

Measurement.

INSTITUTIONS

Use them to align:

Leadership;

People;

Resources;

Systems;

Projects;

Performance.
